<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bad Lobenstein</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lobenstein</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bad Lobenstein is a small spa town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringian-highlands">Thuringian Highlands</a>, in the Saale-Orla district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. From 1647 it was the residence of the counts, later princes, of Reuss-Lobenstein, a branch of the Younger Line of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-reuss">House of Reuss</a>, until the line died out in 1824. Its medieval castle ruin and later palace survive, and the town is now known for its spa.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bad-lobenstein.jpg" alt="Bad Lobenstein" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Sander · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Altstadt_Bad_Lobenstein.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
